## Quick start

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml up --build
```

| What | URL |
|---|---|
| Health check | http://localhost:8000/api/ping/ |
| Django admin | http://localhost:8000/api/admin/ |
{% if use_wagtail %}
| Wagtail admin | http://localhost:8000/api/cms/admin/ |
{% endif %}
{% if rest_api == "DRF" %}
| Swagger (staff only) | http://localhost:8000/api/docs/ |
{% endif %}

Create a superuser:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml run --rm django python manage.py createsuperuser
```

## Tests

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run --rm django pytest
```

Fixtures live in `{{ slug }}/conftest_plugins/` and are registered in the root `conftest.py`.

## Linters

```bash
uvx prek install          # git hook
uvx prek run --all-files  # manual run
```

## Dependencies

Managed by uv, `uv.lock` is the source of truth (Docker images use `uv sync --locked`).

```bash
uv add <package>   # then rebuild the images
```

## Environment
{% if use_s3 %}

- `USE_S3=True` stores media in S3-compatible storage (`AWS_*` variables in `.envs/.production/.django`),
  `USE_S3=False` keeps media on the local filesystem.
{% endif %}
- Database settings come from `POSTGRES_HOST`, `POSTGRES_PORT`, `POSTGRES_DB`, `POSTGRES_USER`, `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`.
- `.envs/.local/` is committed, `.envs/.production/` is never committed.
